 "intro_html": "Two Okayama dishes from the Seto Inland Sea, put together: <b>takomeshi</b> — rice cooked with octopus, ginger and dashi — and <b>iidako no nitsuke</b>, baby octopus simmered in sweet soy. Half the octopus cooks in the rice; the other half is glazed and <b>folded through</b> so every bite has pink and glossy pieces inside. Triangles with a nori strip — no topping. Shaping basics are on the <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri page</a>.",
