    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 8,
   "part": "Sweet-soy baby octopus",
   "part_id": "part-sweet-soy-baby-octopus",
   "time": "3–5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>3–5 min</span>",
   "title": "Reduce to a glaze",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>When the rice is done, tip in the glazed octopus with any leftover glaze and the green onion.</li><li>Fold through gently with the paddle, cutting through the rice rather than mashing it — every scoop should have pink and glossy pieces.</li><li>Let it cool for a few minutes, until it's warm enough to hold.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-9",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Fold the glaze and onion into the rice",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Fold the glazed pieces and green onion through with the paddle — cut, don't mash.",
      "src": "illustrations/baby-octopus-onigiri/9-how1.webp?v=68f40238c7"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/baby-octopus-onigiri/9.webp?v=c608c9646e",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 9,
   "part": "Shape",
   "part_id": "part-shape",
   "time": "~7 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~7 min</span>",
   "title": "Fold the glaze and onion into the rice",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"1\" data-f=\"stalk|stalks\" data-n=\"1\">1 stalk</span>",
     "name_html": "Green onion"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Wet your hands and rub a pinch of salt over your palms.</li><li>Take about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"90\" data-s=\"0\">90 g</span> of the mixed rice (a sixth of it) in your left palm.</li><li>Press the triangle: right hand bent into a “mountain” on top, left hand cupping, turning a third each time — light, so it stays airy (see the <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri page</a>).</li><li>Wrap a nori strip round the bottom. Repeat for six.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-10",
